  "@id": "https://w3id.org/pices/odis/records/zenodo-23568356.jsonld",
  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "RMIS: Catch & Effort Database 4.0",
  "description": "The Catch & Effort Database is an on-line database that houses catch & Effort and Location data. Using the Query System 4.0 application, the user is allow to build a query by catch & effort and location codes. The user is then allowed to optionally preview the result set row by row, and run a RMIS formatted report of their chose using the result set. The report may then be returned to the browser, or sent to a user-entered email address. Review the RMIS Web Site User Manual for detailed description of the database and the web application.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To assist the Pacific Salmon Commission's Working Group on Data in the development of CWT data exchange formats.",
